{%- set T = i18n[lang or "en"] %}
{%- set metaT = T[pageKey] if pageKey else null %}
{%- set pageTitle = title or (metaT.title if metaT) or (site.name + " — engineering roadmaps") %}
{%- set pageDescription = description or (metaT.description if metaT) or site.tagline %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ lang or "en" }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ pageTitle }}</title>
  {#- Search snippets clamp around 155 chars; social cards are roomier. Only the
      SERP description is shortened, so the card keeps the full thesis line. #}
  <meta name="description" content="{{ metaDescription or pageDescription }}">
  {#- The error page is not a page: it must never claim canonical status (every
      real 404 response is served with this body, so a self-canonical here points
      crawlers at an indexable 200 URL) and its noindex must not depend on the
      pre-launch flag, or launch day turns it into an indexable soft-404. #}
  {%- set isErrorPage = page.url == "/404.html" %}
  {%- if not isErrorPage %}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}">
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if i18nSlug %}
  {#- The locales point at each other and x-default points at English — the
      source-of-truth locale. Only chrome pages carry a pair; roadmap content
      pages are English-only because their source is each repo's README. #}
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="{{ site.url }}{{ i18n.en.paths[i18nSlug] }}">
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="ru" href="{{ site.url }}{{ i18n.ru.paths[i18nSlug] }}">
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="{{ site.url }}{{ i18n.en.paths[i18nSlug] }}">
  {%- endif %}
  {% if site.noindex or isErrorPage %}<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">{% endif %}

  {%- set ogSlug = roadmap.slug if roadmap else "default" %}
  {%- set ogImage = site.url + "/assets/og/" + ogSlug + ".png" %}
  <meta property="og:type" content="{{ "article" if roadmap else "website" }}">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ site.name }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ pageTitle }}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ pageDescription }}">
  {%- if not isErrorPage %}
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}">
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if roadmap.updated %}
  <meta property="article:modified_time" content="{{ roadmap.updated }}">
  {%- endif %}
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ ogImage }}">
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
  {%- set ogAlt = (roadmap.title if roadmap else site.name) + " — " + site.tagline %}
  <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ ogAlt }}">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ pageTitle }}">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ pageDescription }}">
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ ogImage }}">
  <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="{{ ogAlt }}">

  {%- set sd = { pageType: pageType, roadmap: roadmap, site: site, pageUrl: page.url, lang: lang or "en", title: pageTitle, description: pageDescription, homePath: T.paths.home } | structuredData %}
  {%- if sd %}
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ sd | jsonLd | safe }}</script>
  {%- endif %}

  <link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon-32.png" sizes="32x32" type="image/png">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/favicon-180.png">
  {#- Fonts are preloaded, not merely declared. Without this the browser only
      discovers them after it has parsed the stylesheet and matched a rule, which
      under load is late enough that the swap lands after first paint and reflows
      the text: measured 0.0513 CLS on a roadmap page, one paragraph losing a
      line 3.6s in. Preload starts the fetch while the HTML is still parsing, so
      the real face is usually there before anything is painted.
      `crossorigin` is required even same-origin — fonts are fetched in CORS
      anonymous mode, and a preload without it is a second, unused download.
      Three files now, not five: the display serif is gone, and the variable sans
      serves body text AND every heading weight from one download — its wght axis
      runs to 700, which is measured, not assumed. Mono is still two files because
      it carries milestone ids and the stamps, which are mono 600 above the fold. #}
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/plex-sans-var.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/plex-mono-400.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/plex-mono-600.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/styles.css">
  <script>
    // Dark mono is the theme, so the default needs no attribute and no work: the
    // stylesheet's :root IS the dark theme. Only a reader who has PICKED light
    // (or picked dark back) carries an attribute, and it is applied before paint
    // so their choice never flashes. With JS off the site is dark, which is
    // the same thing it is with JS on and nothing chosen.
    (function () {
      try {
        var t = localStorage.getItem('proofstone:theme');
        if (t === 'light' || t === 'dark') document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', t);
      } catch (e) {}
    })();
  </script>
</head>
<body data-page="{{ pageType or 'page' }}"{% if roadmap %} data-roadmap="{{ roadmap.slug }}"{% endif %}>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header">
    {#- Mark + wordmark lockup. The SVG is inlined (≈300 bytes, saves a request)
        and carries the same chiseled-P as the favicon/OG/avatar so the identity
        is one object everywhere. aria-hidden + the link's aria-label keep it a
        single named landmark, not a second focus target announcing nothing.
        The fills go through the TOKENS — a literal hex here is the one element
        a palette change could not reach. #}
    <a class="brand" href="{{ T.paths.home }}" aria-label="proofstone — home">
      <svg class="brand__mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect width="32" height="32" rx="7" fill="var(--accent)"/>
        <path fill="var(--bg)" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8.5 9.3L10.3 7.5L21.7 7.5L23.5 9.3L23.5 15.7L21.7 17.5L13.5 17.5L13.5 22.8L11.7 24.5L10.3 24.5L8.5 22.8Z M13.5 10.6L20 10.6L21.3 11.9L21.3 13.1L20 14.4L13.5 14.4Z"/>
      </svg>
      <span class="brand__word">proof<span>stone</span></span>
    </a>
    {#- The sections. Community is deliberately absent: no page exists yet, and a
        nav entry without a page is a promise the site does not keep — the same
        honesty rule that leaves PLANNED cards unlinked. #}
    <nav class="site-links" aria-label="Site sections">
      <a href="{{ T.paths.roadmaps }}"{% if page.url == i18n.en.paths.roadmaps or page.url == i18n.ru.paths.roadmaps %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ T.nav.roadmaps }}</a>
      <a href="{{ T.paths.projects }}"{% if page.url == i18n.en.paths.projects or page.url == i18n.ru.paths.projects %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ T.nav.projects }}</a>
    </nav>
    <span class="site-header__spacer"></span>
    <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Main">
      {%- if i18nSlug %}
      {#- <details>, not a JS dropdown: with JS off it still opens, and the
          entries are ordinary links between the static locale pages. SVG flags,
          not emoji — Windows renders flag emoji as bare letter pairs. #}
      <details class="lang">
        <summary aria-label="Language: {{ T.label }}">
          <span class="lang-btn">
            {%- if lang == "ru" %}
            <svg class="lang-flag" viewBox="0 0 18 13" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect width="18" height="13" fill="#fff"/><rect y="4.33" width="18" height="8.67" fill="#0039a6"/><rect y="8.67" width="18" height="4.33" fill="#d52b1e"/></svg>
            {%- else %}
            <svg class="lang-flag" viewBox="0 0 18 13" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect width="18" height="13" fill="#1a3775"/><path d="M0 0l18 13M18 0L0 13" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.6"/><path d="M0 0l18 13M18 0L0 13" stroke="#c8102e" stroke-width="1.1"/><path d="M9 0v13M0 6.5h18" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="4.3"/><path d="M9 0v13M0 6.5h18" stroke="#c8102e" stroke-width="2.6"/></svg>
            {%- endif %}
            <span>{{ (lang or "en") | upper }}</span><span class="lang-caret" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <ul class="lang-menu">
          <li><a href="{{ i18n.en.paths[i18nSlug] }}"{% if lang != "ru" %} aria-current="true"{% endif %}><svg class="lang-flag" viewBox="0 0 18 13" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect width="18" height="13" fill="#1a3775"/><path d="M0 0l18 13M18 0L0 13" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.6"/><path d="M0 0l18 13M18 0L0 13" stroke="#c8102e" stroke-width="1.1"/><path d="M9 0v13M0 6.5h18" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="4.3"/><path d="M9 0v13M0 6.5h18" stroke="#c8102e" stroke-width="2.6"/></svg>English</a></li>
          <li><a href="{{ i18n.ru.paths[i18nSlug] }}"{% if lang == "ru" %} aria-current="true"{% endif %}><svg class="lang-flag" viewBox="0 0 18 13" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect width="18" height="13" fill="#fff"/><rect y="4.33" width="18" height="8.67" fill="#0039a6"/><rect y="8.67" width="18" height="4.33" fill="#d52b1e"/></svg>Русский</a></li>
        </ul>
      </details>
      {%- endif %}
      {#- A word, not a glyph. It names the theme it switches TO, and the
          accessible name contains that same word (WCAG 2.5.3, Label in Name).
          app.js rewrites both together. Shipped saying "light" because dark is
          the default — with JS off that is the true state, and the button is
          honestly inert. #}
      <button type="button" class="theme-toggle" aria-label="Switch to light theme">light</button>
      <a class="btn-star" href="{{ site.org }}" rel="noopener">{{ T.nav.star }}</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  {#- tabindex="-1" is what makes "Skip to content" actually move focus: without
      it the browser sets the hash and leaves focus on <body>, so a screen
      reader's cursor never travels. Chromium's tab order compensates; Safari and
      several AT pairings do not. #}
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    {#- This line is a promise, so it tracks what the site actually does: the
        negative claims that survive are stated, the vendor is named so a reader
        can go and check rather than take our word. #}
    <p>{{ T.footer.line1Html | safe }}</p>
    <p>{{ T.footer.line2Html | safe }}</p>
  </footer>

  <script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script>
  {#- Analytics. Cookieless by construction: Umami stores nothing on the client,
      so the footer's "no cookies" stays literally true and no consent banner is
      owed. It is the only third-party byte this page loads — fonts, styles and
      app.js are all self-hosted, and every other external URL here is a link the
      reader may follow, not a request the browser makes.
      Placed here rather than in <head> as the vendor suggests: with `defer` the
      two are equivalent, and this file's rule is that <head> carries only what
      must run before paint — the theme script and JSON-LD — while behaviour that
      can wait ships at the end of <body>.
      `data-domains` pins collection to the live host. Without it every local
      `eleventy --serve` session and every preview build would report into the
      same dashboard as real visitors, and launch-day numbers would be mostly us.
      Kept on one line on purpose: the shape of this tag is asserted verbatim by
      tools/proxy-check.mjs, and wrapping it would break that comparison. #}
  <script defer src="https://cloud.umami.is/script.js" data-website-id="eff26170-20d5-4083-ba7b-cdf715ee6e31" data-domains="proofstone.dev"></script>
</body>
</html>
